a timer called clock.
To check.
    a number called waited is the clock's elapsed in milliseconds.
    If waited is greater than or equal to 50 then, Print "waited at least 50 milliseconds".
    Otherwise, Print "waited only {waited} milliseconds".
    a number called 'whole seconds' is the clock's elapsed in seconds.
    If 'whole seconds' is less than 1000 then, Print "and under a thousand seconds".

Start the clock.
Wait 50 milliseconds.
check.
check.
